## 1️⃣ CUSTOMER vs CONSUMER ⭐⭐⭐⭐

### 📖 Definitions

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Customer** | The person who **purchases or pays** for a product/service |
| **Consumer** | The person who **uses or consumes** the product/service |

### 🎯 The Golden Exam Line
> **A customer CAN be a consumer, but a consumer NEED NOT be a customer.**

### 💼 Business Scenarios

| Scenario | Customer | Consumer |
|---|---|---|
| You buy coffee and drink it yourself | You ✅ | You ✅ |
| You buy coffee for your brother | You ✅ | Your brother ✅ |
| A parent buys a toy for their child | Parent ✅ | Child ✅ |
| A company buys pens for its employees | Company (Procurement) ✅ | Employees ✅ |

> 🧠 **Memory Trick:** **Customer = Cash** (pays money out). **Consumer = Consume** (uses the product).

### 🔥 PYQ Comparison Table

| Customer | Consumer |
|---|---|
| Pays for the product | Uses the product |
| Buyer | User |
| May or may not consume it | May or may not pay for it |

> ⚠️ **Exam Tip:** A very common trick question gives a gifting/B2B scenario and asks you to identify who is the customer and who is the consumer separately. Always ask: "Who **paid**?" → Customer. "Who **uses** it?" → Consumer. Don't assume they're always the same person.

