## 2️⃣ MARKETING vs SALES ⭐⭐⭐⭐

```
   MARKETING                          SALES
   "Get them interested"              "Close the deal"
        |                                  |
   Creates AWARENESS                  SELLS the product
        |                                  |
   💸 CASH OUTFLOW                    💰 CASH INFLOW
   (spend on ads, campaigns)          (revenue collected)
        |                                  |
   Happens BEFORE                     Happens AS the
   the purchase                       final transaction
```

| Feature | 📢 Marketing | 🤝 Sales |
|---|---|---|
| **Core function** | Creates awareness | Sells the product |
| **Cash flow direction** | Outflow (spending on ads/promotions/campaigns) | Inflow (revenue collected) |
| **Focus** | Promotion | Revenue |
| **Timing** | Before selling | Final transaction |

> 🧠 **Memory Trick:** **Marketing = Money Goes Out. Sales = Money Comes In.** If you remember only one thing about this pair, remember the cash direction — it's the most tested distinction.

> ❌ **Common Mistake:** Students often use "Marketing" and "Sales" interchangeably in casual speech, but in an exam they are **opposite ends of the cash flow**, not synonyms. Never write "marketing means selling" — that conflates two distinct activities.

