## 6️⃣ VALUE PROPOSITION ⭐⭐⭐

> **Definition:** A statement explaining **why customers should buy your product** over alternatives.

**Example:** *"Best quality at an affordable price."*

> 🧠 **Memory Trick:**
> **Price = What you PAY.**
> **Value = What you GET.**
> A strong value proposition makes the customer feel they're getting more Value than the Price they're paying.

---

## 7️⃣ SELLING PROCESS: PRODUCT vs SERVICE ⭐⭐⭐

```
   Seller  ───provides Offerings───►  Buyer
```

Offerings can be:
- **Products** (tangible)
- **Services** (intangible)
- Or a mix of both

| 📦 Product | 🛎️ Service |
|---|---|
| Tangible (you can touch it) | Intangible (you experience it) |
| Mobile phone | Banking |
| Pen | Consultancy |
| Laptop | Transport |

> 🧠 **Memory Trick:** If you can drop it on your foot, it's a **Product**. If you can't touch it but still benefit from it, it's a **Service**.

